<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  ⚠️⚠️ THE ONE KEY THIS FILE EXISTS FOR, AND WITHOUT IT NOTHING REACHES THE RAIL.

	  The Glamatic is a Siemens S7-1200, and its built-in web server terminates TLS with an old
	  protocol version, weak ciphers and no forward secrecy. App Transport Security rejects all of
	  that by default, and it rejects it BEFORE the URLSession delegate is ever asked about the
	  certificate — so `PLCTrustDelegate` accepting the self-signed cert is necessary and not
	  sufficient. Every request to https://192.168.1.2 simply fails.

	  `NSAllowsLocalNetworking` lifts the ATS requirements for local/link-local destinations ONLY:
	  RFC1918 addresses, .local, and unqualified hostnames. Anything on the public internet is
	  still held to the full policy, which is why this is the correct switch rather than
	  `NSAllowsArbitraryLoads`.

	  PivotBooth (AuraBooth) has carried this key the whole time. ArmControl did not, which is a
	  difference that CANNOT show up in the simulator: the simulated rail never opens a socket.

	  ⚠️ The project uses GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE, so every other key still comes from the
	  INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings and is merged into this file at build time. Do not move those
	  in here, and do not delete this file to "tidy up" — ATS has no INFOPLIST_KEY_ equivalent
	  because it is a dictionary.
	-->
	<!--
	  ⚠️ Required for `LocalNetworkPermission` to work AT ALL.

	  Its detection is a Bonjour browse, and iOS refuses to browse a service type the app has not
	  declared here. Without this entry the browse fails for a reason that has nothing to do with
	  permission, and the check reports a denial that is not real — sending an operator into
	  Settings to fix a switch that was never off.

	  Nothing publishes this service. The rail is a Siemens PLC on a fixed IP and speaks no
	  Bonjour; the type exists purely so there is something legal to browse for.
	-->
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_armcontrol._tcp</string>
	</array>
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
